{44800}{Foreigners are unwelcome in Malicorne, and even the city's own inhabitants are not free to leave.}
{44820}{A woman escaped from Malicorne and now lives somewhere nearby.}
{44840}{The mayor of Malicorne has declared magicians outlaws. His men persecute them even beyond the city walls.}
{44860}{Professor Quentin Blafard disappeared after making a mysterious discovery. His wife suspects that the Malicorne authorities were involved.}
{44880}{They say the soldier stationed at the bridge is rather fond of the bottle...}
{44900}{A man suspected of sorcery is in prison awaiting execution.}
{44920}{The bandit Neril Tenduil is wanted for theft. A reward of 200 coins is offered for his capture, dead or alive. Inquire with the First Sergeant of the city guard.}
{44940}{The mayor recently closed the old mine.}
{44960}{A traveling merchant named Dr. Julius Maximus has set up near the inn. He claims his elixir can cure all manner of fatigue...}
{44980}{Neril Tenduil stole Ernesto Mendego's pendant at the three-tree crossroads south of Malicorne. He was last seen heading for the caves farther south.}
{45000}{Golim Dradoc cannot see a thing without his spectacles. According to the innkeeper, the din of the steam machinery in his workshop must be making him deaf as well.}
{45020}{Ever since the magician Erwin Cornebrume was executed three months ago, no one has been willing to buy his house.}
{45040}{Malicorne's physician told me that the dying half-ogre I encountered suffers from acute Meliotonitis. The remedy is a mushroom called the Trompelamort, which is said to grow in the old mine.}
{45060}{Jacques Trowbridge studies and keeps jars of voracious wood-eating insects called wingless polyopterans. Merely setting their jar on wood excites them enough to escape and devour the wooden surface in minutes!}
{45080}{Golim Dradoc is known to be a man of considerable influence.}
{45100}{By some accounts, Dr. Julius Maximus's Elixir is remarkably effective.}
{45120}{Madam Lil's establishment in Tarant has reportedly closed.}
{45140}{A priest named Dante has reportedly been seen near Malicorne.}
{45160}{Malicorne was built upon the ruins of an ancient city.}
{45180}{My arrival in the city did not go unnoticed.}
{45200}{Malicorne's club is reserved for the city's leading citizens.}
{45220}{Foreigners are unwelcome in Malicorne, and even the city's own inhabitants are not free to leave.}
{45240}{Malicorne's merchants sell their goods to everyone, but they refuse to buy anything from a foreigner.}
{45260}{As long as the bridge provides a route outside Malicorne, the mayor will keep the old mine closed, for it too leads beyond the city's borders.}
{45280}{The ingredients needed to cast Erwin Cornebrume's spell�a vial of dragon's blood and a vial of elven spring water�are said to lie within the old mine.}
{45300}{The magician Erwin Cornebrume was imprisoned and executed one week before the day I traveled into the past.}
{45320}{Several passages have collapsed in the old mine. It is closed until further notice.}
{45340}{Some say the hotel manager and Irina Petroff are having an affair.}
{44901}{The guard arrested a magician within the city itself! He was plotting against the mayor!}
{44921}{A reward of 200 coins is offered to anyone who brings back the bandit Neril Tenduil, dead or alive.}
{44941}{The mayor has closed the old mine. No one is permitted to approach it.}
{44961}{A traveling merchant has parked his wagon behind the inn. He supposedly sells an elixir for every sort of fatigue. A charlatan, if you ask me...}
{45001}{Do you know Golim Dradoc? They call him Squinty Golim because he cannot see a thing without his spectacles! They say he even wears them to bed! And he must be going deaf from the din of all that steam machinery. If he ever left his workshop, one could break into his chest without being heard�the noise would cover everything!}
{45021}{Ever since the magician Erwin Cornebrume was executed three months ago, no one has been willing to buy his house. People seem wary of the place...}
{45081}{Do you know Golim Dradoc? They say his influence reaches far... That must come in terribly handy when he needs to scratch his backside...}
{45101}{Ever since I tried Dr. Julius Maximus's Elixir, my migraines have vanished! That doctor is a saint!}
{45121}{They say Madam Lil's establishment in Tarant has closed!...}
{45141}{Long ago, I met a priest named Dante at the Sour Barnacle in Black Root. They say he has recently been seen in these parts...}
{45161}{Did you know that Malicorne was built upon the ruins of an ancient city? Entrances to tunnels can still be found here and there, leading to old, partially collapsed cellars.}
{45181}{A suspicious individual reportedly arrived in the city not long ago. An illegal entrant, no doubt. Someone rather like you...}
{45201}{[He looks you over contemptuously.] This club declines further every day. They truly will admit anyone now...}
{45241}{Malicorne's merchants conduct trade only with local residents. If you are not from here, they will gladly sell you their goods, but they will never buy anything from you...}
{45301}{Erwin Cornebrume was executed for sorcery a week ago. Yet he belonged to Malicorne's old nobility and was a pure-blooded human!...}
{45321}{Several passages have collapsed in the old mine. It is closed until further notice.}
{28000}{It seems that the Town Gossip might know something about the Mummy. Apparently he is over at the Inn.}
{28020}{According to the Book 'The Story of Amtut', a local Sheep Farmer on the outskirts of town attacked the Mummy.}
{20521}{Old Jongle Dunne the hedgewizard has been acting weird.  Seems to have started just after Constable Owens bought the old steam engine.}
{20581}{You seen City Hall, yet?  Kinda fancy for a place like Shrouded Hills.  A long time ago, it was a Panarii Temple, but for some reason they stopped using it.}
{21041}{Do you follow politics much, friend?  Well, it seems that Caladon is considering joining the Unified Kingdom!  Imagine that!}
{21481}{I heard an old adventurer passing through here the other day.  I don't know what he found, but I heard him mention these coordinates: 617W, 528S.}
{21881}{If you're traveling the hills northwest of Stillwater, watch out for old Drog Blacktooth, the ogre.  He's mostly harmless, but you never know with ogres...}
{24080}{Rumor has it that Mr. Merton Vorman had a bastard, half-ogre son.  He's purportedly buried behind the Vorman Manor, in the family mausoleum.}
{24081}{Have you heard the rumors about Merton Vorman?  It’s said that the mausoleum behind his house holds his bastard, half-ogre son!}
{24100}{Rumor has it that something strange has happened in Ter'elon, an elven village located in the Erriwind Forest to the north.  Qin'ar, the leader of the village, has come to Vormantown to speak with Merton Vorman.}
{24101}{Word has come down from the Erriwind Forest…something strange has happened in the elven village of Ter'elon!  Qin’ar, their leader, has come here to speak with Merton Vorman!}
{24120}{Rumor has it that Veryk Ironwill, the king of the Stone Heart Clan, has come to Vormantown.  No one seems to know why.}
{24121}{Did you see who came into town?  Veryk Ironwill, the king of the Stone Heart Clan!  Word has it he’s staying up at Merton Vorman’s mansion, but no one knows why he’s here!}
{24140}{Rumor has it that Mr. Shackleford takes care of all of Mr. Vorman's personal affairs.}
{24141}{Have you met Mr. Shackleford?  He's Mr. Vorman's lawyer, and takes care of all of his personal affairs.  He's quite an individual!}
{24160}{Rumor has it that Merton K. Vorman founded Vormantown as some sort of "social experiment".}
{24161}{Mr. Vorman founded Vormantown almost 10 years ago...he called it a "social experiment", I think, but I don't know much about things like that...}
{24200}{Strange beasts have been seen wandering the local woods and caves.  The townspeople think it is a sign of Minra's evil.}
{24201}{Have you heard of the strange beasts?  All different forms have been seen wandering the woods and caves of late.  It is a sure sign that Minra's evil is spreading!}
{24220}{The town of Stillglade has a deadly curse upon it.}
{24221}{Steer clear of the town of Stillglade in your travels, stranger.  An evil witch cursed the town many years ago and the entire town died a slow and painful death.  It is said the curse remains to this day.}
{24240}{Kallen is a powerful necromancer that the townspeople say I should avoid.}
{24241}{Have you come across Kallen in your travels?  Quite a powerful necromancer, he is...  But what a twisted sense about him!  Watch out for that one, if you value your sanity!}
{24260}{I should be wary of groups of Minra's soldiers along the main roads.}
{24261}{Groups of Minra's soldiers have been spotted along the main roads.  Stay out of their way, if you know what's good for you.}
{24280}{The evil and powerful witch Minra has imprisoned the queen and taken over the throne in the capital city of Tyr.}
{24281}{Have you heard about the evils taking place in Tyr, the capital city?  Our queen has been imprisoned by the powerful witch Minra.  I have heard that evil began to spread like a plague the moment Minra took the throne!}
{40860}{Randver told me that Loghaire disappeared into the caverns of the Dredge, an old system of dwarven mines that now houses an assortment of foul creatures.}
{41380}{Gunther Willhelm told me that Alexander is a direct descendant of  Saint Mannox.}
{42800}{Edward Willoughsby appointed me the mediator between Tarant and Caladon in the negotiations concerning Caladon's membership into the United Kingdom.  He told me to travel to Caladon and meet a man named Renard in front of the Royal castle.  Renard is to counsel me further concerning the negotiations once I've arrived.}
{42860}{Heinrich Jenks has contracted you to kill King Farad of Caladon.  If you receive an appointment from Edward Willoughsby as mediator of the negotiations between Tarant and Caladon, you are to enter the royal castle, find the kitchens and speak to man named Vernon.  He will instruct you further.  Otherwise, you are to speak with a man named Bullors at the Caledonia's docks, and he will get you into the castle where you can then meet Vernon.}
{42880}{Heinrich Jenks has contracted you to kill King Farad of Caladon.  You are to meet a man named Bullors at the Caledonia's docks.  Apparently, this Bullors will sneak you into the castle, where you are to find a man named Vernon in the royal kitchens.  Vernon will instruct you further.}
{43400}{I have been told that Fawn can give me master training in healing.  She can be found in Quintarra.}
{43500}{Hieronymous Maxim has told me that if I were to bring him a hunting rifle, a loading mechanism, and a revolver chamber he would construct me a mechanized gun.}
{43840}{I found a promissory note from a man named named Elmer Burbottom to Wesley, Lillian Misk's butler.  The note, which promised Wesley 500 coins, was unspecific as to what the payment was for.}
{44580}{I just learned of a Cattanese halfling legend about a spider-demon called Merow Vortahm. The story goes that it is able to cloud your mind and make you believe it's actually a beautiful human woman. Posing as a woman who is lost, it comes to an isolated farm, sizes up the available food supply, then finds a dark place close by to lay her eggs. Her offspring have the same ability to charm people and have no trouble overwhelming the farm. It's just a legend, of course.}
{44600}{There's a large necropolis just north of Monaco on Cattan.}
{44620}{The island of Cattan was known as Kai'tan's Abode in ancient times. An interesting bit of trivia.}
{44640}{The Plainwicke Plantation has an infestation of magickal creatures known as Merow Vortahm. The creatures are trapped on a river island, but that won't last much longer.}
{44680}{Merow Vortahm is not the last of her kind on Cattan.}
{24060}{There seems to be a haunted hunting lodge just up the road from Lynchbany. It could be a good base of operations in this area.}
{24061}{There seems to be a haunted hunting lodge just up the road from Lynchbany. It could be a good base of operations in this area.}
{44380}{There seems to be a haunted hunting lodge just up the road from Lynchbany. It could be a good base of operations in this area - once I get rid of the ghosts, of course.}
{44400}{The entertainers for the Brandybuck fair are late coming to town.}
{44420}{The promoter of the Brandybuck fair is worried the others may have taken a wrong turn and met some bandits. Perhaps I should go help the little fellows out.}
{44440}{Farmer Maggot is extremely protective of his potatoes. I've been advised to give him a wide berth.}
{44460}{Mr. Dakia Foghat is sweet on a traveling-show lass named Leeka Newba. I'm sure he's much too old for her, but who am I to judge if a fellow tries to recapture his youth with a younger woman?}
{44480}{The Shire of Brandybuck has the dual honour of being the largest halfling community and their sheep produce the softest wool in the land.}
{44500}{The town of Leahbo cannot call itself a shire anymore. Something to do with too many "longshanks", the larger races, living there.}
{44520}{Leeka Newba does not like Dakia. She's convinced he's too old for her.}
{44540}{Until this day, I had always assumed the expression "Kill them with kindness" to be just a figure of speach. Today I met a woman named Weqia Rurrae who showed me otherwise. If anyone could do this, it would be her!}
{44560}{There is a small farm for sale in Brandybuck.}
{44660}{The creature known as Merow Vortahm had a very tramatic childhood as a slave to barbarian halflings, which accounts for her psychotic hatred of them.}
{44700}{}
{44720}{A man who lives along the shore of Ivory Lake has informed me that one of the unusual qualities of the lake is that teleportation spells do not work once you leave the shoreline. Curious.}
{44740}{At least one group of Elves have taken offence to other people moving too close to the Glimmering Forest. I need to use caution when I travel through the region.}
{44760}{The town of Marcyona should be getting quite a bit of new business now that a forgotten bridge across the river has been rediscovered.}
{30000}{The belongings of Professor Siegfried were distributed among the people present at his funeral: the antique dealer, the castellan, the gardener. There was a fine helmet, a precious pendant and a pair of valuable gloves.}
{30020}{The Barman hides in the cellar a domestic animal that swallows everything and anything. The people of the mansion are looking for it to hunt it.}
{30040}{The son of Golim the antique dealer is a little rascal. He counterfeited his father's writing to make a fake note addressed to his schoolmaster. He has a real forger talent, according to his father...}
{30060}{According to the manor cook, among the close friends of the wife of the castellan (the gravedigger, the gardener and the bartender), one was often with her. Some half-elf.}
{30080}{According to my companion, the bartender, a man called the Master of Tears seeks the tears of his beloved, Niniel the Gentle.}
